Title: The Last Light
Credit: An original scene for CUE
Author: CUE

INT. OLD LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

Rain ticks against the glass. A lamp turns slowly above them.

MARA
Tell Ellis I'll come tomorrow.

THEO
Tomorrow? The boat leaves at seven.

MARA
(quietly)
I really don't think we should be doing this right now.

THEO
You said that yesterday. And yesterday, and yesterday.

MARA
I never loved her.

THEO
I didn't ask whether you loved her. I asked whether you'd stay.

MARA
But I—

THEO
Don't start that again.

MARA
Wait. Wait. Give me the key.

THEO
The key is on the table. Beside the letter from Ellis.

MARA
Then leave the light on. I'll find my way back.

THEO
I always do.

The lamp passes over the empty doorway.

INT. OLD LIGHTHOUSE - DAWN

The rain has stopped.

THEO
You came back.

MARA
I said I would.

THEO
Is Ellis coming?

MARA
No. Not today.
